# Director gate-signing key — EXAMPLE ONLY (this file is committed; the real key is not).
#
# Do NOT put a real secret here. Generate the real key with:
#
#     python3 automation/approve_gate.py init-key
#
# That writes .governance/.gate_key (mode 600), which is gitignored. The gatekeeper
# uses it (or the DOW_GATE_SECRET environment variable) to verify gate approvals.
#
# Until a key exists, EVERY gate is treated as closed (fail-closed by default), so a
# freshly-cloned template blocks all writes to execution/ until a human creates the key
# and signs the relevant gate with automation/approve_gate.py.
#
# For headless / CI Directors: instead of a key file, export
#     DOW_GATE_SECRET=<64-hex-char secret>
# in the environment where you run approve_gate.py. Keep it out of the repo and logs.
